diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 85e7c82..261aec0 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -41,0 +42,38 @@ toolchain experiment and bypasses the active pin.
+## Shared worktree cache
+
+`workbench.json` records the project identity and complete compiler-install hash.
+Keep it in version control with the wrappers. Checkouts of the same project use
+`$XDG_CACHE_HOME/mylang/workbench` (normally `~/.cache/mylang/workbench`); an
+absolute `PCB_SHARED_CACHE` overrides this location. A new worktree on this
+machine can immediately run the commands above with the existing pin. On a new
+machine, register the matching complete installation with
+`tools/update-toolchain.sh /path/to/install` first.
+
+Source snapshots, compiler installations, native caches, test receipts and final
+executables are shared by content. Identical sources and build inputs reuse the
+same executable and test receipts across worktrees. CPU scheduling width is not
+a build input: changing `PCB_BUILD_JOBS` preserves the executable. Each compiler
+pin gets its own native-cache namespace, so upgrading one checkout cannot evict
+another pin's warm generation. An upgrade changes only that checkout's
+`workbench.json`; review and commit that change deliberately. `.mylang/current`
+is a compatibility link, not the source of the pin.
+
+Concurrent identical builds lock before compiling and publish only successful
+outputs. Test invocations keep reports in each checkout's `.workbench/results`;
+application journals remain at the requested checkout-local path. New or changed
+sources still need compilation/test validation, and `--force` intentionally runs
+tests again. The first migration to the shared snapshot path may revalidate old
+test receipts once. Snapshots currently capture flat `guest/*.my` inputs and the
+test inventory; extend the snapshot contract before adding other compile inputs.
+
+Leave `CACHE` unset normally. If set for an experiment, native caches are placed
+under `$CACHE/<compiler-pin>/<build|tests>`; use `PCB_SHARED_CACHE` to isolate the
+entire store. There is no automatic pruning of whole toolchain pins or executable
+snapshots. Treat published installations and snapshots as immutable; use the
+installer to register different contents instead of editing the shared store. Never clear the shared store while agents are running; clearing it
+makes every checkout cold. Per-pin native generation cleanup remains enabled.
+
+Wrapper regression checks are `tests/workflow.sh` and
+`python3 tests/shared_cache.py`; the latter creates isolated Git worktrees and a
+private shared store, without changing the production cache.
+
